%% caption: What happens from double-clicking the game until a lot is on screen. Steps 3 and 4 are inferred from class names (TS1ObjectProvider, TS1NeighbourProvider, GameController.EnterGameMode).
sequenceDiagram
  actor You
  participant Win as Simitone.Windows
  participant Loc as Game locator
  participant Con as Content loader
  participant Scr as Game screen
  participant Sim as Rules engine (VM)
  participant Wld as World drawing
  You->>Win: start Simitone.Windows.exe
  Win->>Loc: where is The Sims 1 installed?
  Loc-->>Win: registry path, or the default Program Files folder
  Win->>Con: load objects, neighborhoods, sounds from that folder
  You->>Scr: pick a house and press Enter Lot
  Scr->>Sim: build the house and its people
  Scr->>Wld: draw the lot (sprites or 3D)
  loop every frame
    Sim->>Sim: let each object run its behavior
    Wld->>You: show the updated picture
  end
